course: dictionary
lesson: 6555
title: The word next
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Next is a small word with several jobs. It can mean the one that comes right after this one: «Next day he asks politely and plays where they put him» means the day after. It can also mean nearest in place, or beside, as in «sitting right next to him».
explain: Look at the words around next to see which job it does. A time word like day, week or number tells you it means after. A place word, or a person sitting beside someone, tells you it means beside or nearest. Try the meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: As an adverb, next means after this, then. «What happens next?» asks what comes after this point in a story. The clue is the question itself: it is asking about the following event.
fact: Next means the one that comes right after this one.
fact: Next (to) means beside, as in «sitting right next to him».
fact: Next can mean after this or then, as in «What happens next?»
fact: «The Great Sphinx» is carved from the rock «next to the pyramids», so next means beside.
fact: A good check is to swap in another word such as after or beside. If it still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
exercise: «His dad plays a game with him on Sunday mornings, sitting right next to him.» What does next to mean here? | Under | After Sunday | *Beside | Far away from
exercise: «Next day he asks politely and plays where they put him.» What does next mean here? | Very late at night | The day before | *The day after | At the nearest shop
exercise: In the pattern 2, 4, 6, what is the next number? | 7 | 5 | *8 | 10
test: «The next bus leaves in ten minutes.» What does next mean? | *The one that comes right after this one | Red | Broken | The biggest bus
test: «The Great Sphinx is carved from the rock next to the pyramids.» Where is the Sphinx? | Miles away from the pyramids | On top of the sea | Inside the pyramids | *Beside the pyramids
exam: «What happens next?» Which meaning fits best? | The one before | Beside | *After this, then | Last of all
